Z||000006||Standard||06-01-2001||12:02 AM||||I got a ton of those one-liners.. there's a bunch of 'em in an old thread here somewhere..<P>Never promise to complete any project within six months of the end of the year, in either direction.<P>Theory is when you know everything and nothing is working. Organization is when nothing is working and everyone knows why. Practice is when everything is working and no one knows why.<P>There's nothing so small that it can't be blown out of proportion.<P>The only time to be positive is when you are positive you are wrong.<P>Murphy's Law #6 - If anything simply cannot go wrong, it will anyway.<P>Murphy's Law #7 - If you perceive that there are four possible ways in which a procedure can go wrong, and circumvent these, then a fifth way, unprepared for, will promptly develop.<P>Murphy's Law #8 - If everything seems to be going well, you have obviously overlooked something.<P>Murphy's Law #10 - If several things that could have gone wrong have not gone wrong, it would have been ultimately beneficial for them to have gone wrong.<P>Murphy's Law #11 - It is impossible to make anything foolproof because fools are so ingenious.<P>Murphy's Law #15 - Complex problems have simple, easy-to-understand wrong answers.<P>When you get your tang tongueled around your eye tooth, you can't see what you are saying!<P>Matter will be damaged in direct proportion to its value.<P>The number of people watching you is directly proportional to the stupidity of your actions.<P>All things being equal, all things are never equal.<P>If there is a 50/50 chance of something going wrong, nine times out of ten it will.<P>Murphy was an optimist.<P>Murphy was a bloody optimist.<P>Bare feet magnetize sharp metal objects so they always point upwards from the floor - especially in the dark.<P>The more ridiculous a belief system, the higher the probability of its success.<P>When you're up to your nose in it, keep your mouth shut.<P>If you're feeling good, don't worry.  You'll get over it.<P>If everything seems to be coming your way, you're probably in the wrong lane.<P>The man who can smile when things go wrong...has thought of someone he can blame it on.<P>At some time in the life cycle of virtually every organization, its ability to succeed in spite of itself runs out.<P>When a man's wife learns to understand him, she usually stops listening to him.<P>Most jobs are marginally better than daytime TV.<P>Whatever hits the fan will not be evenly distributed - Also known as the 'How Come It All Landed On Me Law'.<P>It is a mistake to allow any mechanical object to realize that you are in a hurry.<P>Inside every small problem there is a large problem struggling to get out.<P>Friends may come and go, but enemies accumulate.<P>A woman never forgets the men she could have had; a man, the women he couldn't.<P>Common sense is not that common.<P>Beauty is skin deep, but ugly goes right to the bone.<P>Justice always prevails ... three times out of seven.<P>When working on a project, if you put away a tool that you're certain you're finished with, you will need it instantly.<P>Any tool, when dropped, will roll into the least accessible corner of the workshop. - Corollary:<BR>On the way to the corner, any dropped tool will first strike your toes.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000007||Tweek||06-02-2001||12:34 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Standard:<BR><B><BR>When working on a project, if you put away a tool that you're certain you're finished with, you will need it instantly.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Too true<BR> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR><B><BR>Any tool, when dropped, will roll into the least accessible corner of the workshop. - Corollary:<BR>On the way to the corner, any dropped tool will first strike your toes.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>If you were unlucky enough to drop it over your engine bay it will NOT find its way to the ground.<P>||||reg||1
